{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1516989-the-corts-seelie-and-unseelie","id":1516989,"title":"The Corts Seelie and Unseelie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-02T12:11:39-07:00","id":1516989,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Corts Seelie and Unseelie","content":"From what I understand, kiths tend to differ depending on which cut they are part of, I have a general idea of how each cut works, the problem is that I have a certain difficulty in visualizing how certain kiths behave in each cut, so I wanted to hear from someone who understands more about the subject.<br /> <br /> Boggans: I know what a Seelie would look like, but I can't imagine how an Unseelie Boggan would behave.<br /> <br /> Eshu: In their case, I only imagine that the Unseelie are more flexible in terms of laws, but in general I don't know exactly what differentiates one from the other.<br /> <br /> Nockers: I can't even figure out how to tell one from the other, to me they all seem a bit grumpy.<br /> <br /> Pooka: This one I have a general idea, but I wanted to know how far an Unseelie Pooka goes, I know they are prone to deception, but I wanted to know how far, I imagine something similar to a vampire, but reduced.<br /> <br /> Red Caps: I know that a Seelie Red Cap has a higher seal of honor, but this weak explanation seems more like a squire than a troll.<br /> <br /> Satyrs: What's the difference between a Seelie and an Unseelie? Shame?<br /> <br /> Selkies: This one I have no idea.<br /> <br /> Piskies: Also have no idea.<br /> <br /> Sluagh: This is one I fail to understand, I know most are Unseelie, but what are Seelie like?<br /> <br /> Swan Maidens: Are the Unseelie Yanderes?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T13:43:50-07:00","id":1516994,"title":"","content":"(Probably Part 1)<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll try to go off the top of my head on some of these and speculate as to what these manifestations might be like. For sake of reference I\u2019ll add this:<br /> <br /> <b>Seelie</b> Code: Death Before Dishonor, Love Conquers All, Beauty is Life, Never Forgive A Debt<br /> (The Seelie are partially inspired by the genre of fairy stories where the fay are alien but recognizably humane with happy and well ordered courts that seem charming and benevolent to humanity; although beneath the surface they are just as capable of alien morality but seem more orthodox and acceptable)<br /> <br /> <b>Unseelie</b> Code: Change is Good, Glamour is Free, Honor Is A Lie, Passion Before Duty<br /> (The Unseelie are partially inspired by the genre of fairy tales where the fay are actually sinister and fairly likely to harm humanity. They may not be malevolent in the way a witch or demon might be, but they\u2019ll hurt people all the same. That said they do have their own rules and one can get by if you discover and make use of them. The courtly Unseelie Fae do resemble the Seelie albeit having goblins, orcs, and gremlins as hangers on rather than brownies, pixies, and gnomes).<br /> <br /> <b>Boggan</b><br /> The typical Boggan (invoking Hobbits, Brownies and miscellaneous house, cottage, &amp; hearth spirits) is of the Seelie Court (imagine the bucolic peasants and townsfolk of the Good King\u2019s fantasy realm). Boggans have a somewhat conservative ethos that cares for the sanctity of traditions which protect and uphold family, society, and laboring on good works. That\u2019s the Beauty and Good for a Boggan. All the needy deserve a helping hand and the warmth of the hearth.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie Boggan is typically the Boggan who\u2019s been abused by others. Whether by society in general or someone in particular, the Boggan has been dislodged from their place of modest content. They have seen that the society they so care for \u2018is a lie\u2019. The good die young, the generous are taken advantage of, and most people are stupid and cruel. Unseelie Boggans work for themselves first (and maybe a few trusted friends\u2026) and don\u2019t let themselves be \u2018tricked\u2019 into helping others anymore. They lash out with subtle barbs, clock-work revenge, and acidic gossip. They still fully understand how society works, they simply no longer have rose-tinted glasses. However, despite all of this, deep down the Boggan still cares. Even the most cynical Unseelie Boggan of the Shadow Court, if they happened upon Tiny Tim at Christmas, would be sorely tempted to leave an anonymous gift of fresh clothing and good food for the Pruitt\u2019s. This is the road that leads most Unseelie Boggans to eventually return to the Seelie Court.<br /> <br /> <b>Eshu</b><br /> The Eshu are a tricky kith because they have a lot going on. On one hand they are clearly inspired by a particular real-world spirit and like a lot of early WW they are torn between invoking the trappings of that cultural heritage and a more archetypal role. I don\u2019t feel competent to comment on the former so I\u2019ll focus on the latter.<br /> <br /> From an archetypal perspective the Eshu have a few niches that they take from imo, niches which often overlap somewhat with others kiths (particularly Sidhe &amp; Piskies). They are fundamentally wanderers and so are associated with luck, trickery, and a certain just-so quality, along with wisdom. I\u2019d say the Archetypal Eshu is the Mysterious Wise Wanderer who meets the Hero several times along their Journey (or serves as an impromptu squire) and provides advice, exposition, assistance, guidance, and wisdom all under an enigmatic veil (which can only ever be revealed at the end of the story where it turns out they\u2019re the Heroes\u2019 lover in disguise [Sheik from Zelda would be a good Eshu I just realized] or are one of the Grateful Dead or are the Sage in disguise or the Heroes long-lost-brother, or something). Of course the Eshu has a Wise Person vibe in that they fulfill a Bardic/Troubadour role and of course both of the latter, despite the flippantly associated with them, have also been long associated with keepers of secrets, mysteries, lore, and wisdom. The Eshu has something in common with the wandering trickster and rightful heir in disguise archetypes tbh but imo those roles are better suited to Piskie/Clurichauns for the former and Sidhe for the latter. That preamble aside I think the Eshu are a real toss up between Seelie and Unseelie, where the role doesn\u2019t much change but the context and vibe does.<br /> <br /> The Seelie Eshu is the more playful and positive sort. They know how to face death-defying odds with a swashbucklers panache and that no fight is too dangerous not to wink at you boyfriend before doing something really cool. They know the sacred law of the wandering gods/angels - those who are kind to mysterious guests are rewarded, those who are cruel (or selfish) get punished. The Seelie Eshu is the perfect chivalric troubadour, charming pirate rake, and encouraging\u2014and-worldly sidekick to your Sidhe Romeo/Juliet figure. <br /> <br /> The Unseelie Eshu is the capriciousness of the open roads where bandits, pirates, and charlatans reign. They\u2019ve seen that Society and Seelie living is a useless straight jacket invented by cynics and accepted by fools. The Unseelie Eshu has no hesitation about unsavory tactics, in fact she eagerly uses them all: deception, theft, sleight of hand, open violence (and threat of violence), etc. Of course the Unseelie Eshu retains their theatrical instincts. The Unseelie Eshu Phantom Thief may pull off an ingenious heist and never be seen - but he can\u2019t help leave behind a mocking calling card. The Unseelie Eshu Bandit Princess can\u2019t help but pause to taunt the foolish goody-two-shoes Seelie squires trying to catch her. <br /> <br /> The Eshu is ultimately a kith of the wanderers wisdom and a certain type of guile hero savant charm. A thought I had while writing this is that the classical hero Odysseus (the ingenious master of disguise and deception who can\u2019t help reveal himself in his moment of triumph over his enemies despite the potential consequences) is a good example of an Eshu. It\u2019s also important to note imo that Seelie Eshu are probably even more vicious than Unseelie when it comes to punishing those who violate the rites of travelers and hospitality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T13:52:56-07:00","id":1516996,"title":"","content":"Well technically there\u2019s the Seelie, Unseelie and Shadow Court.<br /> <br /> Seelie and unseelie are largely still Kithain but their moral compass differs, the Seelie Courts see ripping glamour from a mortal as heinous whereabouts the Unseelie see ravaging, using mortals and acts of cruelty as perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> However both Courts are still Kithain so on the brighter side of the Dreaming, so the Unseelie could be seen as the morally greyer counterparts of the Seelie.<br /> <br /> Appearance wise they are essentially the same apart from personal style, trappings and darker chimera for the Unseelie.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the Thallain who are the darker counterparts to the Kithain, they are the twisted evil reflections and the shadow court, not only are their forms savage Grimm fairytale reflections but their innate powers are different.<br /> <br /> Any Kithain can twist or fall becoming a Thallain and joining the Nightmare Dreaming, however due to their moral ambiguity and willingness to commit cruel destructive acts particularly on mortals the Unseelie are far closer to becoming Thallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T14:48:53-07:00","id":1517002,"title":"","content":"(Part 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Nockers</b><br /> The Nockers are inspired by the particular fairy tale of knockers in the Cornish tin mines. That\u2019s not all however. They also draw on the genre of \u2018Nuisance Fairies\u2019; the ones who tie hair into knots, knock loudly in the night, bump things over, or make machines break down. They\u2019re subterranean Kobolds, mining Knockers, household Hobgoblins, and modern Gremlins. They\u2019re also in a certain Punk/Underground Comic aesthetic, the sort of thing that would later be associated with WoW Goblins or in WoD the Ratkin with Saw Launchers.<br /> <br /> The typical Nocker is Unseelie but both kiths have unifying qualities. They are all driven around the bend by their neurotic desperation to express their inner vision and genius in a flawed and incomplete world. Every Nocker is fueled by bone-deep resentment. You could kind of imagine them as if Richard Nixon or Tyrion Lannister were trapped in the body of a Christmas Elf. Nockers are tiny and wimpy; easily kicked around by any Redcap, Orge, or Squire who can get their hands on them. The typical Nockers will end up like Warhammer Goblins, having to attach themselves to whoever is willing to fight anyone else who tries to abuse them in exchange for mining and inventions and so on. Of course they all yearn for the day that their genius is finally recognized, they are embraced by the important and beloved people, and everyone strongman who ever taunted them was forced to admit their intelligence. Of course even the most accomplished Nocker will never actually be satisfied - their vision of perfection is impossible to realize but they\u2019ll never be able to fully accept that.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie Nockers are the above without any frills. They curse loudly and openly loath and disdain everyone else: all of the stupid rules of society that try to restrain them. From the stupid Sidhe who make the rules to help themselves to the stupid Trolls &amp; Squires who enforce it to the stupid Redcaps who bully anyone smarter than them to the stupid Boggans who are too dumb to realize that it\u2019s dumb to be happy (and all the stuff they make is boring and crap). Nockers chafe at any attempt to restrain their creative impulses and will go to any lengths to gather the materials necessary to complete them; however hazardous or unethical. Nothing matters as long as they can create what they imagine will get them the accolades they deserve.<br /> <br /> The Seelie Nockers are the minority and are as neurotic as their Unseelie kin but with a few particular nuances attached. Most Seelie Nockers are those who have decided that adopting some parts of the Seelie way to better organize themselves - not all leading Nockers are Seelie of course but it\u2019s useful when you have to temporarily restrain everyone\u2019s passions for some common cause - organizing patent leagues to avoid feuds, organizing chimerical mines, organizing Nocker revolts, etc. The focus on self-denial in favor of a set of codes that have the interest of the many in mind can be quite useful for them. Some Nockers are not so cynical - they truly want to be part of the happy society of the Good King\u2019s realm which the Seelie seem to be. These Nockers will often struggle to sand down their edges - trying to restrain themselves to kid-friendly expletives (\u201cOh muzzle-nuggets!\u201d) and trying to believe the sort of things that Boggans and Sidhe seem to believe. Results are hit-and-miss. Many Seelie Nockers feel true happiness sharing their toys with children or being part of something larger than themselves - but the deck is stacked against them. Other kiths know the Nocker\u2019s by reputation and expect them to eventually revert (why trust a Nocker with something sensitive if a Boggan or Troll is available?). They also know that Nocker craft will inevitably self-destruct, it\u2019s a matter of when not if. On top of all this, the Nockers are natural critics. No matter how badly they want to believe, they\u2019ll naturally turn every molehill into a mountain and overlook the good things (of course sometimes they\u2019re also the only ones willing to acknowledge real mountains). The treatment they receive from others and the inevitable conclusion that the Good Society they hoped for is fundamentally flawed, most Nockers will cynically retreat into their Unseelie roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T15:17:07-07:00","id":1517007,"title":"","content":"(Part 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Pooka</b><br /> <br /> The Pooka are inspired by both the particular story of the Pooka\u2019s wild ride but more generally also Animal-fables and prankish and trickster fairy tales. On one hand the Pooka will embody animal qualities reminiscent of Aesop\u2019s Fables and twisting human social mores into a funhouse mirror version with animal characteristics. Similarly the Pooka embody the archetype of the fairy prankster, trickster, and mischief maker; try as you like they will tie knots in your hair, make funny noises, tie your shoelaces together, tell silly limericks, and all that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Like the Eshu I don\u2019t think the Pooka are particularly predisposed to either the Seelie or Unseelie Courts. It\u2019s a toss up. The Pooka are also incredibly diverse - following the suit of their animal self. They do have some common traits however. They all have an even deeper level of non-rational thinking than other fey, being tied to animal logic and intentional subversion of even Changeling mores. The Pooka are often associated with jesters and clowns, those who intentionally subvert conventional logic and reason. The Pooka do not simply lie or tell untruths, they follow a logic all their own. They also all have a sort of animal magnetism or animal sense - for some reason people feel naturally inclined to trust and like them, sharing things with them they otherwise wouldn\u2019t. Perhaps it\u2019s because people naturally sense that the Pooka are distinctly separated from society as they understand it, making it allowable to confide in them - after all, what\u2019s the harm in confiding with a dog? Who\u2019s it going to tell? <br /> <br /> The Seelie Pooka are typically associated with cute, fluffy, and nice animals. Pets, barnyard animals, cute critters, etc. Seelie Pooka are also more likely to adopt some type of role in social life, even if it\u2019s an informal one of their own creation. Whatever their role they will technically fulfill it to the tee - but always in a way that\u2019s so bizarre and unorthodox it makes one question the premises of the duties in the first place - but of course, as natural comedians, the average Pooka doesn\u2019t question stupidity but rather embraces it with gusto and joie de vivre. The Pooka will embrace Beauty and Love the same way; Krazy Kat, Pepe La Pou, these are both classical Pooka lovers - what matters to the typical Pooka is not being dashing or suave (although they can be) but rather being an undeniable burst of passionate love and affection that is completely without self-regard or self-consciousness; the Pooka is never afraid of looking ridiculous. (The tragic thing is that Pooka often struggle to have their feelings be believed by others; direct confessions are impossible or clearly farcical so many are forced into indirect methods of showing affection). This is a key tragedy of the Pooka in general. Their nature gives them a truly unique perspective - but at the cost of their unbridgeable separation from all non-Pooka. Finally the Seelie Pooka never forgets a debt. This can be two-fold: the spurned hound who never forgets who slighted those it loves or the vicious animal-monsters of horror movies where once one has polluted, littered, or otherwise soiled nature the hounds of hell are unleashed in nature red, tooth and claw.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie Pooka has much in common with their Seelie cousin and Pooka are probably fairly fluid where Court is concerned. The most significant distinction being the matter of society. The Seelie Pooka is inevitably apart of society, despite knowing at their core how alien to it they are. The Unseelie Pooka makes no such pretensions. It is not part of society as other changelings imagine it; it is as free and wild as any beast could hope for. Unseelie Pooka have no love, not even playful love, for the orderliness of the established world - it\u2019s all nonsense designed to hold back the primordial waves of nature and chaos ultimately. The Unseelie Pooka feels no compunction against taking what they please: glamour or otherwise; eat or be eaten, steal or be stolen from. Any attempt to get the Pooka to accept some principle other than its own internal nature is a lie and a deception; however many flowers they put on the collar and chain, it\u2019s still a collar and chain. Do What Comes Naturally, this shall be the whole of the Law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T17:22:25-07:00","id":1517015,"title":"","content":"(Part 4)<br /> <br /> <b>Redcaps</b><br /> <br /> Redcaps, like many kith, are inspired both by a specific fairy tale as well as a general vibe. In particular they\u2019re inspired by the Redcaps who haunt the peel towers of northern England and Scotland. In general they\u2019re inspired by the more brutal and visceral sort of bogey. They are inspired by the tales of horrors that eat up bad children, bellow in the night to terrorize, break things wantonly, drag the unsuspecting into the water, and chase the unwary through the dark forests.<br /> <br /> Before we continue, this leads to a natural question, \u2018Why are the Redcaps not Thallain\u2019? This is a fair question. tbh they probably should have been, retroactively speaking. However imo the original writers wanted a scary kith as an option to embody those sorts of themes and so the Redcaps (&amp; Slaugh) made it into the playable kiths. That said, how do we justify them? My take is that while the Redcaps are closer to Nightmare than any other kith, they sit just on the edge without crossing the line. They are the (relatively) controlled horror. Even more than that, they are Thrill. They\u2019re exciting, they\u2019re dangerous; they\u2019re not meant for small children, old people, or polite society. They are Thrill, Danger, &amp; Terror just barely kept within the limits of the Dreaming. They aren\u2019t doing it for Nightmare\u2019s sake but to embody a necessary, albeit unsettling, part of the healthy psyche. The pressure valve that prevents the true Nightmares from festering. After all, Redcaps may be frightening and dangerous, but they can be kept to an acceptable level. Their terribly competent Thallain cousins, the icy cannibal Ghouls, cannot have the same said of them. <br /> <br /> All that being said, the typical Redcap is Unseelie. The Redcaps by nature occupy the cutting edge. They have a deep hunger within them, one which can never be fully filled or satiated. This is not only a physical hunger but an emotional and spiritual one. Sure, Redcaps are also always literally hungry, just enough to add a little shiver to their threats to \u201cgobble you up\u201d. They\u2019re also hungry in every other way. They need excitement, thrill, adrenaline. Redcaps are in an arms race to out-do each other in outrageous presentations - leather jackets and tattoos are kid stuff. Try putting rivets into your flesh. Try filing your teeth into points. Try ripping up your ears to look like a street cat. Try slicing your tongue into a fork. Don\u2019t just think it\u2019s physical either. Watch the Knight squirm when you tell him where to stick his Lance. Dare that Satyr to put her horns where her mouth is. Do anything. As long as you can feel that wonderful thrill of having dared further and truly affected the world.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie Redcap, the typical and majority of Redcaps, are the unfettered above. They have no particular affection for anything in the world - with maybe a few exceptions they all accept that everything must one day be eaten. Feel free to like Old Tom and his antics, but don\u2019t act shocked about how he got blown away by some hunter with a shotgun - it\u2019ll happen to you too and hell, you\u2019ve probably done the same. Speaking of - glamour is free. Glamour is everywhere. Every Changeling and Chimera is a walking sack of the stuff, just waiting to be toasted golden-brown. The mortals? Every last one of them is ready to scream their heads off when you grab their ankles from a sewer grate - all that glamour is free for the taking. Anything that tries to stop you from fulfilling that instinctual drive, that shark impulse to keep going, to keep feeding and feeling that thrilling buzz; it\u2019s a con. Don\u2019t stop. If you stop, you die. That\u2019s all the Seelie Code is. A net they lay to tie you up and when you stop moving, you die. <br /> <br /> The Seelie Redcaps are few and part of this is that they must reckon with something their Unseelie cousins simply embrace as given - perhaps because it\u2019s too painful to really think about<b></b>: everyone is scared of them. It doesn\u2019t matter what you say or do, what you look like or how you act, it\u2019s all the same - they can all see the glint in your eye and the gleam of your teeth, they can tell you\u2019re dangerous even if they can\u2019t imagine how the hunger really feels. No Redcap chose their hunger, their endless and relentless hunger, but that doesn\u2019t matter. No one trusts a shark. No one trusts a Redcap. Even your best friends will always flinch when you move a bit too quickly. It\u2019s a hard life, especially for the kids. It\u2019s easier to embrace it than to fight it. The hunger gets so much easier if you work with it. When you stop struggling you can just focus on how good it feeds to eat and eat and eat and eat and let that cover the pain. That\u2019s why, ultimately, most Redcaps will end up giving up and return to the Unseelie way.<br /> <br /> What about the few who stick it out though? Those semi-mythical \u201cWhite Caps\u201d? Well, they have to be gluttons for punishment and have impeccable resolve. Which actually makes the first tenet of the Seelie Code relatively easy. The Unseelie Redcap coils from the notion, the walking stomach cares only for survival, it can\u2019t eat if it\u2019s dead. The typical White Cap, on some level, has embraced death. Death would make the hunger stop after all. It\u2019s almost cathartic to imagine - dying in an indisputably honorable fashion - both symbolically and literally destroying your relentless hunger. Love and Beauty are hard for the White Caps. They inspire revulsion and dread. So for most of them, they resign themselves to love and admire from afar. Most courts with a White Cap have a few Sidhe who are totally unaware of the silent zeal of their private champions - they\u2019ll never know that the mysterious masked knight who challenged the rake who insulted them was a White Cap admirer in disguise. Now it\u2019s true that some are attracted to frightening visages, particularly Slaugh and Nockers - but even than many White Caps are too afraid of their own hunger to risk consumption of love, preferring the self-denial of chivalric romance. The last tenet of the Seelie Code is where the boundless repression of the White Caps receive an outlet. While it is a cruel and self-fulfilling prophecy that leads many courts to make their White Caps executioners or marshalls, it\u2019s undeniably effective: when the White Cap has a sanctioned outlet for their repressed energies they become a terrifying and unstoppable machine of execution. This also is considered something of the ultimate test of a Seelie Cap: how long can they manage to restrain themselves to the letter of Justice before slipping and bloodying their cap on the condemned? A White Cap is only a white cap as long as it\u2019s pristine - a single drop of blood brings about its end.<br /> <br /> Most Redcaps are or become Unseelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T14:30:36-07:00","id":1517102,"title":"","content":"(Part 5)<br /> <br /> <b>Satyrs</b><br /> <br /> Satyrs are inspired by both a particular example and an archetypal role. On one hand they\u2019re obviously inspired by Satyrs &amp; Fauns; the bawdy beast-men of classical antiquity. They\u2019re also more generally inspired by two related principles: one by spirits of indulgence, excess, festivity, and passion as well as by spirits representing a beast-man unity which is communion with the liminal state between them. In the former case comparisons can be made with Fay Beauties although those are more typically Sidhe, whereas Satyrs and their ilk are the entertainers and ringleaders of such gatherings. In the latter case a comparison could be made with Pooka; the distinction is that Satyrs are Beast-Men while Pooka are Fairy Beasts who are sometimes in the shape of men. Satyrs have a role akin to Centaurs, Satyrs, and the classical Werewolf; they retain a fundamentally human aspect while having unfettered animal energies and impulses.<br /> <br /> IMO the Satyrs are another toss up kith, not particularly inclined to either the Seelie or Unseelie path, or maybe having a slight inclination towards the Unseelie. Fundamentally the Satyrs are all animal energies and passions flowing without limit. They are the maenads of the Bacchanalia. They induct the sacred mysteries of passion by dancing in the cave mouths or on the hill tops. These mysteries can be taken into many forms but their basis is the core of animal passion - feeling, pleasure, consumption, etc. Satyrs are capable of indulging in art, theater, music, and poetry but all ultimately for the sake of passion, excess, and catharsis. Satyrs would have no use for technical mastery which does not rouse the humors somehow. Satyrs are also inclined to draw others into their celebrations, being social amongst one another as well as spreading their revels to all bystanders they can.<br /> <br /> The Seelie Satyr is likely to struggle with the first tenet of the Code most of all - how can a creature of such vivacity accept death? Seelie Satyrs who survive tend to do so by finding aspects of honor which can become synonymous with their passions - the Satyr Knight whose passion is for chivalric romance, to dishonor his oaths would be to trample upon the passions which form the basis for his life, making death acceptable. While cases like the above certainly exist, the majority of Satyrs would rather take the Unseelie Way than die. The other tenets of the Seelie Code however present far fewer difficulties. Few kiths care more for Beauty and Love than the Satyrs. Romance and trust, peon and ode; the forces of Beauty &amp; Love overwhelm (and sometimes destroy) all Satyrs. No court who hosts Satyrs can be a stranger to the regular declarations of love and devotion which fall readily from the lips of a Satyr - whether to the highest Sidhe Prince or the lowliest Boggan Kitchen Maid (or even a Nocker Chimney Sweep or Slaugh Plumber). The last tenet is no issue for the average Satyr either. The frenzy of Dionysus and Pan is never far from them - their passions seek satisfaction to slights and so vengeance is often ready at hand. Somewhat more difficult can be to repay good with good - many Satyrs are happy to take, take, take, and only give back by accident. They don\u2019t mean anything by it, but it\u2019s hard for them to tear themselves away from their pleasure buttons.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie Satyr is actually quite similar to their Seelie cousin although without the courtly pretensions or the ridiculous notion that anything would possibly be worth dying for. The Unseelie Satyrs thrive in the bacchic manias which disintegrate social bonds and links, all custom and etiquette and established order must bow in favor of their pleasures (and everyone else ought to come around to their way of seeing things too\u2026). Like pleasure, glamour is free for the taking. Every person is a reservoir and are just ready to be drawn to the camping ground for the revels. Sure, perhaps some revelers won\u2019t be able to keep up with the Satyrs and will end up drained, but there\u2019s more where they came from. No reason to stop the party! Anything that gets in the way of the party is pointless moralism. Honor, duty, those are all distractions. Do as you will and if it feels good than it is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}